  "slug": "end-structural-df64",
  "summary": "Recent preprints push foundation models toward raw reads, signals and fused modalities, bypassing count matrices, basecalls and separate-modality pipelines.",
  "synthesis": "The common thread is moving representation learning closer to primary measurements or joint multimodal inputs. scRM pretrains on scRNA-seq reads rather than count matrices, and Brieno tokenizes raw nanopore signal with residual vector quantization for species ID, basecalling and methylation tasks. HistoTx fuses transcript tokens with H&E patches early, at arbitrary spatial transcriptomics resolution, while MorphoProt conditions multiscale histology on RNA to infer spatial protein abundance. HiCP2GAN reuses a pretrained Hi-C Vision Transformer as a GAN discriminator, and PhenoMe offers interpretable exploration of foundation-model microscopy embeddings. RadMultiBench is a cautionary counterpoint: pre-trained vision-language models failed clinical tasks in thoracic and breast imaging. Evidence so far comes from preprints, apart from HiCP2GAN.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-sonnet-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-11-08"
}
